From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:59:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sio: Expose the T8010 PDM receive endpoint

The A10's PDM microphone controller hands its samples to SmartIO on
receive endpoint 0x5b (the "dma-channels" record of the pdm node in the
iPad 6 and iPad 7 Apple device trees). Expose it as a DMA channel next
to the touch and speaker endpoints.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
index 20d135e..fb613ef 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
@@ -1097,10 +1097,14 @@ static const struct apple_sio_hw apple_sio_s8000_hw = {
 	.num_dma_ranges = ARRAY_SIZE(apple_sio_s8000_dma_ranges),
 };
 
-/* SPI3 touch TX and MCA2 speaker TX, independently described by the J71b ADT. */
+/*
+ * SPI3 touch TX, MCA2 speaker TX and PDM microphone RX, each described by
+ * the J71b ADT.
+ */
 static const struct apple_sio_dma_range apple_sio_t8010_dma_ranges[] = {
 	{ 0x1a, 0x1a },
 	{ 0x2c, 0x2c },
+	{ 0x5b, 0x5b },
 };
 
 static const struct apple_sio_hw apple_sio_t8010_hw = {
